        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4c63b6bd-fcb0-57a5-8499-8c7ed29a3844",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ralph Hutchinson, Lorene Rogers\n- Organizations: University of Texas at Austin, Dickinson College, University of New Mexico, Washington & Jefferson College, University of Idaho, Idaho Technical Institute, University of Texas System\n- Places: Austin, Texas, Texas State Capitol\n- Roles: Head football coach, president, biochemist, educator\n- Topics: American college sports, university leadership\n\nFacts:\n- Ralph Fielding \"Hutch\" Hutchinson was born on February 19, 1878, and he was an American football, basketball, and baseball player.\n- The University of Texas at Austin was founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas.\"\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at Dickinson College in 1901.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at the University of Texas at Austin from 1903 to 1905.\n- Lorene Lane Rogers was born on April 3, 1914, and she was an American biochemist and educator.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at the University of New Mexico from 1911 to 1916.\n- Ralph Hutchinson served as head football coach at Washington & Jefferson College in 1918, at the University of Idaho in 1919, and at Idaho Technical Institute from 1920 to 1927.\n- Ralph Hutchinson compiled a career college football coaching record of 61 wins, 53 losses, and 6 ties.\n- Ralph Hutchinson died on March 30, 1935.\n- The University of Texas at Austin is a public research university and the flagship institution of the University of Texas System.\n- The University of Texas at Austin is located in Austin, Texas, about 1 mile from the Texas State Capitol.\n- Lorene Rogers served as president of the University of Texas at Austin in the 1970s and has been described as the first woman in the United States to lead a public university.\n- Lorene Rogers died on January 11, 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9c16e6b9-abaf-5f1b-aa27-ddfeb20405b0",
        "text": "Page: Ralph Hutchinson. Sentence: Ralph Fielding \"Hutch\" Hutchinson (February 19, 1878 – March 30, 1935) was an American football, basketball, and baseball player.\nPage: Ralph Hutchinson. Sentence: He served as the head football coach at Dickinson College (1901), the University of Texas at Austin (1903–1905), the University of New Mexico (1911–1916), Washington & Jefferson College (1918), the University of Idaho (1919), and the Idaho Technical Institute (now Idaho State University) (1920–1927), compiling a career college football record of 61–53–6.\nPage: University of Texas at Austin. Sentence: The University of Texas at Austin (UT, UT Austin, or Texas) is a public research university and the flagship institution of the University of Texas System.\nPage: University of Texas at Austin. Sentence: Founded in 1881 as \"The University of Texas,\" its campus is located in Austin, Texas, approximately 1 mile (1.6 km) from the Texas State Capitol.\nPage: Lorene Rogers. Sentence: Lorene Lane Rogers (April 3, 1914 – January 11, 2009) was an American biochemist and educator who served as the president of the University of Texas at Austin in the 1970s, who has been described as the first woman in the United States to lead a public university.",
